ecutor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. curl remained at its original version despite a newer available candidate, and the lock, OS release, and kernel persisted through a fully evidenced restart. The restart protocol includes a healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, restored system health, and recovered task-specific state.","limitations":["A complete distribution-wide update was not run; update protection was directly tested with `dnf upgrade curl`, supported by the persisted exact versionlock and visible newer candidate.","No separate application service, user-data workload, or multi-node cluster existed to validate during restart recovery; evidence covers system health and the task-specific package and lock state."]}
